{"chunk_id": "0bd89bc9c135", "text": "Ravana crosses the ocean and visits the forest hermitage of the demon Maricha, who has withdrawn into an ascetic life. After being received with ritual hospitality, Ravana explains the disaster at Janasthana: Rama single\u2011handedly slew Khara, Dushana, Trishiras, and fourteen thousand titans, avenging the mutilation of Ravana\u2019s sister Shurpanakha. Burning with anger and humiliation, Ravana unveils a calculated plan for revenge. He intends to abduct Rama\u2019s wife, Sita, believing her loss will destroy Rama with grief. To accomplish this, he asks Maricha\u2014skilled in illusion\u2014to transform into a dazzling golden deer that will lure Rama and Lakshmana away from the hermitage. The scheme marks the fateful beginning of the plot that will lead to Sita\u2019s abduction and the great war to come.\nRavana visits the ascetic demon Maricha and reveals his plan to abduct Sita by using Maricha disguised as a golden deer to lure Rama away.\nThemes: deception and strategy, abduction plot, arrogance of Ravana, looming conflict, loyalty and counsel", "vector": [0.009950648993253708, -0.008340294472873211, 0.012963354587554932, -0.008789852261543274, -0.01709659770131111, 0.01383562944829464, -0.0409030057489872, -0.026262199506163597, -0.023685632273554802, -0.019538968801498413, 0.015955930575728416, 0.01134628988802433, 0.004391571041196585, 0.021323777735233307, -0.007709572557359934, 0.010930282063782215, 0.04149346798658371, -0.01156771369278431, 0.025873029604554176, -0.02596696838736534, -0.007944416254758835, -0.0028231528121978045, -0.0057066939771175385, 0.020277047529816628, -0.023403819650411606, 0.001059311325661838, 0.018935086205601692, -0.028181204572319984, 0.00813229102641344, -0.01176229864358902, -0.004867967683821917, -0.019243737682700157, 0.01392956729978323, -0.013017033226788044, -0.015217850916087627, -0.0038279469590634108, 0.007716282270848751, -0.01629142090678215, 0.007944416254758835, -0.013822210